  "scene": {
    "id": "overlap-pilot3",
    "language": "Okay. So, this situation's going to be thinking about the overlap, where in, uh, a teammate of mine in a further position than me, so for example, if I'm the left back, the right back, this would be the central midfielder, has the ball, and I'm going to run beyond him to create another option, and sort of unsettle the opposition defense with my momentum, and with, uh, you know, a sudden burst forward. Um, so, I'm gonna sort of unpause, run [0]beyond my teammate, (laughs) and he's gonna give [1]me the ball.[2] And at this point, I have a decision to make, because the ball is coming towards me, um, so is the opponent, um, and it's all about, like, how much space do I feel I have in front of me when I receive the ball. It's about getting the ball with a good first [3]touch, and then I can either run straight towards goal and take a shot, or if I feel like this defender's too close to me, I can maybe turn back and give it back to my opponent. In this situation, I've got lots of space, so I'm just gonna drive forward, and maybe have a shot at goal. Um... [4]And, you know, there we go. If I was close enough, then (laughs) uh, we would have scored a goal. But, uh, I'm sure the ball will eventually get there. (laughs)",
